            "committedDate": "2026-08-02T00:34:18.000+02:00",
            "shortMessage": "The window's storage, reached once and guarded once",
            "shortMessageMarkdown": null,
            "shortMessageMarkdownLink": "<a data-pjax=\"true\" title=\"The window&#39;s storage, reached once and guarded once\n\nThree places in the view each did this differently: the read cache wrapped its\nwrites and not its reads, the scheme hook kept its own pair of guards, and the\nsettings store had none, so a window over quota answered a changed setting with a\nrejected promise. All three want storage that cannot throw, because none of the\nways it fails is a reason to refuse to draw a pull request.\n\n`opensInside.ts` decides which links the window keeps and which it hands to a\nbrowser.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;\" class=\"color-fg-default\" href=\"/flazouh/githubpro/commit/4c84c54779112f6f592559f7e023dd540866fcc0\">The window's storage, reached once and guarded once</a>",
            "bodyMessageHtml": "Three places in the view each did this differently: the read cache wrapped its\nwrites and not its reads, the scheme hook kept its own pair of guards, and the\nsettings store had none, so a window over quota answered a changed setting with a\nrejected promise. All three want storage that cannot throw, because none of the\nways it fails is a reason to refuse to draw a pull request.\n\n`opensInside.ts` decides which links the window keeps and which it hands to a\nbrowser.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;",
