            "committedDate": "2026-08-02T00:34:05.000+02:00",
            "shortMessage": "Zoom that survives a launch, and the menu that offers it",
            "shortMessageMarkdown": null,
            "shortMessageMarkdownLink": "<a data-pjax=\"true\" title=\"Zoom that survives a launch, and the menu that offers it\n\n`pageZoom.ts` holds the ladder and the bounds once, so the key handler and the\nmain-process RPC cannot invent two of them. `acrossRuns.ts` keeps the few facts\nabout the window that outlive a run: zoom is a property of the window rather than\nof the page, and it has to be known before the first paint or every launch draws\none frame at the wrong size.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;\" class=\"color-fg-default\" href=\"/flazouh/githubpro/commit/b7988b0b5b7c849b4ab98afa2efeaac74c350751\">Zoom that survives a launch, and the menu that offers it</a>",
            "bodyMessageHtml": "`pageZoom.ts` holds the ladder and the bounds once, so the key handler and the\nmain-process RPC cannot invent two of them. `acrossRuns.ts` keeps the few facts\nabout the window that outlive a run: zoom is a property of the window rather than\nof the page, and it has to be known before the first paint or every launch draws\none frame at the wrong size.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;",
