        "title": "Aug 1, 2026",
        "commits": [
          {
            "oid": "2693988dbfe2aa7453a11aaae56e0946c5c1bd0a",
            "url": "/flazouh/githubpro/commit/2693988dbfe2aa7453a11aaae56e0946c5c1bd0a",
            "authoredDate": "2026-08-01T23:58:44.000+02:00",
            "committedDate": "2026-08-01T23:58:44.000+02:00",
            "shortMessage": "The push runs CI's gates first, and storage stops throwing",
            "shortMessageMarkdown": null,
            "shortMessageMarkdownLink": "<a data-pjax=\"true\" title=\"The push runs CI&#39;s gates first, and storage stops throwing\n\nCI went red on a rule this repo has held for a long time: no try/catch, because\nEffect turns a throw into a failure the type shows. The two that were left both\nwrapped `localStorage`, and they become the same `UndefinedOr.liftThrowable` that\n`remembered.ts` already uses for the same three cases, a private window, storage\nturned off, and a spent quota. The behaviour is what it was, and the reason it is\nsafe is now in the signature rather than in a comment.\n\n`lefthook.yml` runs the linter, the typecheck and the tests before a push, in the\norder `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs them, piped so the first failure stops the\nrest. Nothing new is being checked. The check only moves to where it can still be\nacted on, which is a second of linting against a red branch and a run of CI spent\nsaying so. Lefthook itself comes from Homebrew rather than from `package.json`,\nwhich keeps the workspace lockfile out of it. `LEFTHOOK=0 git push` goes past it.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;\" class=\"color-fg-default\" href=\"/flazouh/githubpro/commit/2693988dbfe2aa7453a11aaae56e0946c5c1bd0a\">The push runs CI's gates first, and storage stops throwing</a>",
            "bodyMessageHtml": "CI went red on a rule this repo has held for a long time: no try/catch, because\nEffect turns a throw into a failure the type shows. The two that were left both\nwrapped `localStorage`, and they become the same `UndefinedOr.liftThrowable` that\n`remembered.ts` already uses for the same three cases, a private window, storage\nturned off, and a spent quota. The behaviour is what it was, and the reason it is\nsafe is now in the signature rather than in a comment.\n\n`lefthook.yml` runs the linter, the typecheck and the tests before a push, in the\norder `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs them, piped so the first failure stops the\nrest. Nothing new is being checked. The check only moves to where it can still be\nacted on, which is a second of linting against a red branch and a run of CI spent\nsaying so. Lefthook itself comes from Homebrew rather than from `package.json`,\nwhich keeps the workspace lockfile out of it. `LEFTHOOK=0 git push` goes past it.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;",
