          {
            "oid": "2e4fa15a3587394c0bf905d6e9be5cddc813415e",
            "url": "/flazouh/githubpro/commit/2e4fa15a3587394c0bf905d6e9be5cddc813415e",
            "authoredDate": "2026-08-01T23:44:17.000+02:00",
            "committedDate": "2026-08-01T23:44:17.000+02:00",
            "shortMessage": "The header's badge matches the well, and the author gets a face",
            "shortMessageMarkdown": null,
            "shortMessageMarkdownLink": "<a data-pjax=\"true\" title=\"The header&#39;s badge matches the well, and the author gets a face\n\nThe badge was a pill above a rectangle, and it began eight pixels to the right of the\nwell beneath it because the row holding it carried padding of its own. It is cut to\nthe same corner and the same padding as the well now, and that row has no padding\nleft: the card&#39;s own inset is what holds both blocks off the border, so the two fills\nstart at the same edge. The controls beside the badge take the same height, since a\nrow of buttons shorter than the badge is the old mismatch moved rather than removed.\n\nThe author&#39;s login gets the face the list already draws for them, from the same `Who`\nas every other person in the interface, so the profile card behind it comes along.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;\" class=\"color-fg-default\" href=\"/flazouh/githubpro/commit/2e4fa15a3587394c0bf905d6e9be5cddc813415e\">The header's badge matches the well, and the author gets a face</a>",
            "bodyMessageHtml": "The badge was a pill above a rectangle, and it began eight pixels to the right of the\nwell beneath it because the row holding it carried padding of its own. It is cut to\nthe same corner and the same padding as the well now, and that row has no padding\nleft: the card's own inset is what holds both blocks off the border, so the two fills\nstart at the same edge. The controls beside the badge take the same height, since a\nrow of buttons shorter than the badge is the old mismatch moved rather than removed.\n\nThe author's login gets the face the list already draws for them, from the same `Who`\nas every other person in the interface, so the profile card behind it comes along.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;",
