      {
        "title": "Jul 31, 2026",
        "commits": [
          {
            "oid": "b39998173cf44ed694a984537121dd3c11c45589",
            "url": "/flazouh/githubpro/commit/b39998173cf44ed694a984537121dd3c11c45589",
            "authoredDate": "2026-07-31T18:44:24.000+02:00",
            "committedDate": "2026-07-31T18:44:24.000+02:00",
            "shortMessage": "Settings from the account menu, and a sheet that sits where it should",
            "shortMessageMarkdown": null,
            "shortMessageMarkdownLink": "<a data-pjax=\"true\" title=\"Settings from the account menu, and a sheet that sits where it should\n\nThree things were wrong with the sheet in the app&#39;s window, and the first is the\none that made it look broken: it was pinned to the top-left corner with its own\nfirst heading under the traffic lights. The browser does centre a modal dialog —\nwith `margin: auto` — and both of these interfaces are built on a reset that sets\nevery margin to zero, so it never centred at all. Centred here instead, where it\ncan be seen and tested.\n\nSecond, it was sized in viewport percentages, which know nothing about what a\nshell keeps in its corners. It now asks: `--sheet-away` is how much room the\nfurniture needs, 76px in a window whose title strip is 38px and nothing on a page\nthat has no strip at all.\n\nThird, `Charac…` beside `Words` and `Off` is a choice a reader has to guess at.\nThe row of choices is wide enough for the longest word any knob offers.\n\nAnd the way in. The sheet came with its own small button, which is right on a\npull request card — the knobs are about how a diff is drawn, and the card is\nwhere a diff is — and left the Working Set, the screen this app opens on, with no\nway into the settings whatsoever. The window holds the sheet now and the account\nmenu opens it, a corner that already answers who you are being where anybody\nlooks for what you have chosen.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;\" class=\"color-fg-default\" href=\"/flazouh/githubpro/commit/b39998173cf44ed694a984537121dd3c11c45589\">Settings from the account menu, and a sheet that sits where it should</a>",
            "bodyMessageHtml": "Three things were wrong with the sheet in the app's window, and the first is the\none that made it look broken: it was pinned to the top-left corner with its own\nfirst heading under the traffic lights. The browser does centre a modal dialog —\nwith `margin: auto` — and both of these interfaces are built on a reset that sets\nevery margin to zero, so it never centred at all. Centred here instead, where it\ncan be seen and tested.\n\nSecond, it was sized in viewport percentages, which know nothing about what a\nshell keeps in its corners. It now asks: `--sheet-away` is how much room the\nfurniture needs, 76px in a window whose title strip is 38px and nothing on a page\nthat has no strip at all.\n\nThird, `Charac…` beside `Words` and `Off` is a choice a reader has to guess at.\nThe row of choices is wide enough for the longest word any knob offers.\n\nAnd the way in. The sheet came with its own small button, which is right on a\npull request card — the knobs are about how a diff is drawn, and the card is\nwhere a diff is — and left the Working Set, the screen this app opens on, with no\nway into the settings whatsoever. The window holds the sheet now and the account\nmenu opens it, a corner that already answers who you are being where anybody\nlooks for what you have chosen.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;",
            "authors": [
