            "shortMessage": "The owner's picture beside a repository's name in the list",
            "shortMessageMarkdown": null,
            "shortMessageMarkdownLink": "<a data-pjax=\"true\" title=\"The owner&#39;s picture beside a repository&#39;s name in the list\n\nA row already names the repository it is in, and the name is the part that has\nto be read: flowline-labs/flowline, octo-org/octo-repo, flazouh/stack-probe\nare twenty characters of monospace that all begin differently and end the same.\nA reader scanning a mixed Working Set for one project&#39;s work was reading every\none of them.\n\nGitHub&#39;s redirect from a login to an avatar answers for an organisation exactly\nas it does for a person, so the picture costs no lookup — the row already knows\nthe owner. Rounded square rather than circle, which is their own distinction and\na useful one on a line that already carries a round face: the circle at the left\nis a person, this is a place. Where they have nothing to serve, the initial\nstands in, because a broken image reads as a fault rather than as an absence.\n\nNot drawn on a single repository&#39;s list, which names itself above its rows.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;\" class=\"color-fg-default\" href=\"/flazouh/githubpro/commit/45495a6bcf4e9ff36ad682ae6e31351ee78154b5\">The owner's picture beside a repository's name in the list</a>",
            "bodyMessageHtml": "A row already names the repository it is in, and the name is the part that has\nto be read: flowline-labs/flowline, octo-org/octo-repo, flazouh/stack-probe\nare twenty characters of monospace that all begin differently and end the same.\nA reader scanning a mixed Working Set for one project's work was reading every\none of them.\n\nGitHub's redirect from a login to an avatar answers for an organisation exactly\nas it does for a person, so the picture costs no lookup — the row already knows\nthe owner. Rounded square rather than circle, which is their own distinction and\na useful one on a line that already carries a round face: the circle at the left\nis a person, this is a place. Where they have nothing to serve, the initial\nstands in, because a broken image reads as a fault rather than as an absence.\n\nNot drawn on a single repository's list, which names itself above its rows.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;",
